# PlayOS input node separation (Sprint 12 — deferred hardening)
#
# The ASUS embedded-controller nodes (event6/7/8; USB 0b05:1abe, reported as
# "Asus Keyboard") carry the Command Center keys (KEY_PROG1/KEY_PROG2), M1/M2,
# brightness, volume, and power/sleep. A game must not read these directly —
# it only needs the gamepad node (Microsoft X-Box 360 pad, 045e:028e, event5).
# The compositor and shell run as root, so they still read the EC nodes.
#
# The gamepad stays in the `input` group (games are in `input`); the EC nodes
# are moved to root:root 0600. The i8042 "AT Translated Set 2 keyboard"
# (event3) is intentionally left in `input`: it carries only volume/power/
# sleep/wakeup (no Command Center / M1-M2), power/sleep are intercepted at the
# seat, and reboot is seccomp-blocked.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="0b05", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1abe", GROUP="root", MODE="0600"
